---
import Legal from '../layouts/Legal.astro';
---

<Legal
	title="Privacy"
	description="Privacy policy for the DesignReady landing page. The site runs without analytics or third-party requests."
>
	<p>
		This is placeholder content and must be reviewed by the site owner before
		the site goes live. It describes the data handling of this landing page,
		not the DesignReady Figma plugin.
	</p>

	<section class="flex flex-col gap-2">
		<h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-text">The short version</h2>
		<p>
			This site is a static page. It loads its fonts locally, uses no
			analytics, sets no tracking cookies, and makes no third-party requests.
			The only data processed is what the hosting provider records to serve
			the page.
		</p>
	</section>

	<section class="flex flex-col gap-2">
		<h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-text">Hosting and server logs</h2>
		<p>
			The site is hosted on Cloudflare Pages. When you open a page, the
			hosting provider processes technical data such as your IP address, the
			requested URL, the referrer, and your browser user agent. This data is
			used to deliver the page and to keep the service secure and stable. The
			legal basis is our legitimate interest in a functioning website under
			Art. 6 (1) (f) GDPR.
		</p>
	</section>

	<section class="flex flex-col gap-2">
		<h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-text">Fonts</h2>
		<p>
			The Inter typeface is bundled with the site and served from the same
			domain. No request is made to Google Fonts or any other third party.
		</p>
	</section>

	<section class="flex flex-col gap-2">
		<h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-text">
			No analytics, no cookies
		</h2>
		<p>
			This site does not use analytics, advertising, or tracking. It stores a
			single value in your browser to remember your light or dark theme
			choice. This value stays on your device and is not sent anywhere.
		</p>
	</section>

	<section class="flex flex-col gap-2">
		<h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-text">External links</h2>
		<p>
			The site links to Figma Community and GitHub. When you follow those
			links, the linked services handle your data under their own privacy
			policies.
		</p>
	</section>

	<section class="flex flex-col gap-2">
		<h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-text">Your rights and contact</h2>
		<p>
			You have the right to access, correct, and delete your data, and to
			object to processing. For any request, contact <a
				href="mailto:design@stefan-holzheu.de"
				class="text-brand hover:underline">design@stefan-holzheu.de</a
			>.
		</p>
	</section>
</Legal>
